## an10.61
an10.61:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, it is said that no prior point of ignorance is found, before which there was no ignorance, and afterwards it came to be. | T: “‘Monks, a beginning point for ignorance—[such that one might say], “Before this, ignorance did not exist; then it came into play”—cannot be discerned.’ This, monks, has been said.
an10.61:1.2 | S: And yet it is evident that there is a specific condition for ignorance. | T: Nevertheless, it can be discerned, ‘Ignorance comes from this condition.’
an10.61:2.1 | S: I say that ignorance is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: And I tell you, ignorance has its food and is not without food.
an10.61:2.2 | S: And what is the fuel for ignorance? | T: And what is the food for ignorance?
an10.61:2.3 | S: You should say: ‘The five hindrances.’ | T: ‘The five hindrances,’ it should be said.
an10.61:2.4 | S: I say that the five hindrances are fueled by something, they’re not unfueled. | T: And I tell you, the five hindrances have their food and are not without food.
an10.61:2.5 | S: And what is the fuel for the five hindrances? | T: And what is the food for the five hindrances?
an10.61:2.6 | S: You should say: ‘The three kinds of misconduct.’ | T: ‘The three forms of misconduct’ …
an10.61:2.7 | S: I say that the three kinds of misconduct are fueled by something, they’re not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.61:2.8 | S: And what is the fuel for the three kinds of misconduct? | T: And what is the food for the three forms of misconduct?
an10.61:2.9 | S: You should say: ‘Lack of sense restraint.’ | T: ‘Lack of restraint of the senses’ …
an10.61:2.10 | S: I say that lack of sense restraint is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.61:2.11 | S: And what is the fuel for lack of sense restraint? | T: And what is the food for lack of restraint of the senses?
an10.61:2.12 | S: You should say: ‘Lack of mindfulness and situational awareness.’ | T: ‘Lack of mindfulness & alertness’ …
an10.61:2.13 | S: I say that lack of mindfulness and situational awareness is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.61:2.14 | S: And what is the fuel for lack of mindfulness and situational awareness? | T: And what is the food for lack of mindfulness & alertness?
an10.61:2.15 | S: You should say: ‘Irrational application of mind.’ | T: ‘Inappropriate attention’ …
an10.61:2.16 | S: I say that irrational application of mind is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.61:2.17 | S: And what is the fuel for irrational application of mind? | T: And what is the food for inappropriate attention?
an10.61:2.18 | S: You should say: ‘Lack of faith.’ | T: ‘Lack of conviction’ …
an10.61:2.19 | S: I say that lack of faith is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.61:2.20 | S: And what is the fuel for lack of faith? | T: And what is the food for lack of conviction?
an10.61:2.21 | S: You should say: ‘Listening to an untrue teaching.’ | T: ‘Not hearing the true Dhamma’ …
an10.61:2.22 | S: I say that listening to an untrue teaching is fueled by something, it’s not unfueled. | T: (none)
an10.61:2.23 | S: And what is the fuel for listening to an untrue teaching? | T: And what is the food for not hearing the true Dhamma?
an10.61:2.24 | S: You should say: ‘Associating with untrue persons.’ | T: ‘Associating with people of no integrity’ [or: ‘not associating with people of integrity’], it should be said.
an10.61:3.1 | S: In this way, when the factor of associating with untrue persons is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of listening to an untrue teaching. When the factor of listening to an untrue teaching is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of lack of faith … irrational application of mind … lack of mindfulness and situational awareness … lack of sense restraint … the three kinds of misconduct … the five hindrances. When the five hindrances are fulfilled, they fulfill ignorance. | T: “Thus, when not associating with people of integrity is made full, it fills [the conditions for] not hearing the true Dhamma. When not hearing the true Dhamma is made full, it fills [the conditions for] lack of conviction. When lack of conviction is made full, it fills [the conditions for] inappropriate attention… lack of mindfulness & alertness… lack of restraint of the senses… the three forms of misconduct… the five hindrances. When the five hindrances are made full, they fulfill [the conditions for] ignorance.
an10.61:3.2 | S: That’s the fuel for ignorance, and that’s how it’s fulfilled. | T: Such is the food of this ignorance, and thus is it made full.
an10.61:4.1 | S: It’s like when the heavens rain heavily on a mountain top, and the water flows downhill to fill the hollows, crevices, and creeks. As they become full, they fill up the pools. The pools fill up the lakes, the lakes fill up the streams, and the streams fill up the rivers. And as the rivers become full, they fill up the ocean. | T: “Just as when the devas pour rain in heavy drops & crash thunder on the upper mountains: The water, flowing down along the slopes, fills the branches of the mountain ravines & gullies. When the branches of the mountain ravines & gullies are full, they fill the little lakes. When the little lakes are full, they fill the big lakes… the little rivers… the big rivers. When the big rivers are full, they fill the great ocean.
an10.61:4.2 | S: That’s the fuel for the ocean, and that’s how it’s filled up. | T: Such is the food of the great ocean, and thus is it made full.
an10.61:5.1 | S: In the same way, when the factor of associating with untrue persons is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of listening to an untrue teaching. When the factor of listening to an untrue teaching is fulfilled, it fulfills the factor of lack of faith … irrational application of mind … lack of mindfulness and situational awareness … lack of sense restraint … the three kinds of misconduct … the five hindrances. When the five hindrances are fulfilled, they fulfill ignorance. | T: In the same way, when not associating with people of integrity is made full, it fills [the conditions for] not hearing the true Dhamma… lack of conviction… inappropriate attention… lack of mindfulness & alertness… lack of restraint of the senses… the three forms of misconduct… the five hindrances. When the five hindrances are made full, they fulfill [the conditions for] ignorance.
an10.61:5.2 | S: That’s the fuel for ignorance, and that’s how it’s fulfilled. | T: Such is the food of this ignorance, and thus is it made full.
an10.61:6.1 | S: I say that knowledge and freedom are fueled by something, they’re not unfueled. | T: “Now, I tell you, clear knowing & release have their food and are not without food.
